{"adjusted_val_bpb": 1.089633816396633, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No integrity problems. The diff changes one line: the std of the token embedding (wte) init goes from 1.0 to 0.5. This is a normal hyperparameter change. It does not touch the val_bpb measurement, the data, the seed lines, the prepare.py import or the evaluation call.", "No bugs that would make the result meaningless. The change only rescales the embedding init. It has no effect on shapes, the training loop or the evaluation.", "I can't recompute z from these numbers. Each side has only one run (candidate 1.0896, incumbent 1.0947), so there is no within-sample variance. The difference is 0.0051 in the candidate's favour. The reported z = 0.660 implies a noise sigma of about 0.0077 that must come from elsewhere, such as an earlier replicate estimate. That is consistent with the numbers, but I can't check it from what was given.", "The provisional reject decision fits a z of 0.66. A single-run gain of 0.0051 is within the noise. If this direction looks worth pursuing, a replicate run would settle it."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Reduce token embedding init std from 1.0 to 0.5 (lm_head init unchanged); since the embedding output is RMS-normed, this mainly makes the Adam embedding updates relatively larger.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": 3, "idea_id": "i025", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 1.0947419228319701, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 1.0947419228319701, "n": 1}, "job_id": "1794364879_SS_01_candidate_7_dad1c170", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.058519600000000005, "cost_usd_plan": 0.058519600000000005, "latency_s": 3.5424826983362436, "requested_model": "sonnet", "role": "coder", "served_model": "sonnet", "tokens_in": 14949, "tokens_out": 386}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0204062, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0204062, "latency_s": 6.550717419013381,